    {"id": "state.scene.current.wing", "family": "wing", "codec": true, "desk": [{"kind": "scene", "scene": 4, "name": "UP1", "via": "native"}], "request": {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/state"}, "response": {"status": 200, "body": {"state": {"scene.current": {"number": 4, "name": "UP1"}}}}, "note": "Slot 13 (27 Oct): the Wing's scene report names the loaded scene (its file, from $active), and scene.current is {number, name}, an object, never a number. A `scene` event carries the same two fields, and a `delta` of path scene.current (a name the desk says after the event, or its file renamed at the same place) carries exactly this value. #342: the Companion module read it with Number(value)."},
