    {"id": "state.trigger.wing", "family": "wing", "codec": true, "desk": [{"kind": "trigger_mode", "trigger": "user:U1.1", "mode": "MIDICCP", "sends": true, "via": "native"}, {"kind": "trigger_mode", "trigger": "user:U1.2", "mode": "OFF", "sends": false, "via": "native"}], "request": {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/state"}, "response": {"status": 200, "body": {"state": {"trigger.user:U1.1": {"sends": true, "mode": "MIDICCP"}, "trigger.user:U1.2": {"sends": false, "mode": "OFF"}}}}, "note": "27 Oct (DEV: ROADMAP): a desk key's assignment is state, one path per trigger: trigger.<id> = {sends, mode}, the id the `trigger` event's, verbatim, everything after the first \"trigger.\" (it may hold dots: user:U1.1). sends true means a press reaches the bridge (the Wing: MIDICCP or MIDINP); false, it doesn't (OFF, a toggle, any other mode); mode is the desk's own word. Pushed whole as a delta on change (a Wing scene stores the keys' modes: recalling one can set them OFF). Absent or null is unknown (the OSC fallback; the native session down): a client says it can't check, never treats it as safe."}
